WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.950
Here's how to make a DualSense look like an Xbox controller to your games.

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.010
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:11.595
On the Dashboard, click Add Controller, and pick Xbox.

4
00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:18.416
Turn on your DualSense, by cable or Bluetooth, and open the Devices page.

5
00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:21.816
Drag the DualSense onto the new controller in the sidebar.

6
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:29.672
PadForge knows the DualSense, so it maps it for you.

7
00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:32.352
Open the controller's Mappings tab.

8
00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:36.152
Cross drives A, Circle drives B, Square X, and Triangle Y.

9
00:00:36.192 --> 00:00:40.442
The sticks, triggers and D-pad go where an Xbox pad has them.

10
00:00:41.848 --> 00:00:45.818
Games now see an Xbox controller, and show Xbox prompts.

11
00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:48.678
A game's rumble still shakes the DualSense.

12
00:00:49.998 --> 00:00:52.768
If a game also sees the DualSense itself,

13
00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:55.588
tick Hide from Games on its panel in Devices.

14
00:00:56.378 --> 00:00:59.648
Once HidHide is installed, PadForge ticks it for you.

15
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:02.755
That's it.

16
00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:04.975
Find more guides at padforge.org.
